Package: GQR
Type: Package
Title: Generalised Q Analysis in R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Gábor", "Pozsgai", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "pozsgaig@coleoptera.hu"),
    person("Tomaz Ponce", "Dentinho", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Implements Generalised Q analysis as introduced by Dentinho,
    Kourtit and Nijkamp (2023) <doi:10.47743/ejes-2023-0201>. The method
    constructs many synthetic combined statements from smaller sets of simple
    ranked or scored statements, forms the synthetic evaluation matrix, applies
    principal component analysis with optional Varimax rotation, and supports
    interpretation through regressions on statement content and respondent
    characteristics. The package provides both a programmatic workflow and an
    optional Shiny interface. A bundled gardening example contains selected
    columns from the multilingual Central and Eastern European questionnaire
    dataset described by Varga-Szilay et al. (2026)
    <doi:10.1038/s41597-026-07887-9>.
